---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const packageJson = `{
  "name": "standardagent-my-workflow",
  "version": "0.3.1",
  "type": "module",
  "main": "./dist/index.js",
  "keywords": ["standardagent"],
  "standardagent": {
    "entryAgents": ["my_agent"]
  },
  "peerDependencies": {
    "@standardagents/spec": ">=0.2.0"
  }
}`;
---

<Base
  title="Publish"
  description="How to publish a Standard Agent package so that the catalogue lists it."
>
  <h1>Publish an agent</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    The catalogue has no accounts and no upload form. Publish a package to npm with the two
    markers below, and it appears here the next time the catalogue is built.
  </p>

  <h2>What the catalogue looks for</h2>
  <ol class="plain-list">
    <li>The keyword <code>standardagent</code> in the package's <code>keywords</code>.</li>
    <li>
      A <code>standardagent</code> field in <code>package.json</code> whose
      <code>entryAgents</code> lists at least one agent.
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p class="lede">
    Both come from the specification's
    <a href="https://standardagentspec.org/latest/distribution/packaging">Packaging</a> page. A
    package with the keyword but without the field is left out.
  </p>

  <pre><code>{packageJson}</code></pre>

  <h2>What an agent's page shows</h2>
  <ul class="plain-list">
    <li>Entry agents, from <code>standardagent.entryAgents</code>.</li>
    <li>Effects and thread endpoints, when the field lists them.</li>
    <li>
      Hooks the agent adds to a parent that composes it, from
      <code>standardagent.parentHooks</code>.
    </li>
    <li>The <code>@standardagents/spec</code> range in <code>peerDependencies</code>.</li>
    <li>Version, licence, publisher, and links, as npm reports them.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Providers and tooling</h2>
  <p class="lede">
    A package that supports agents without being one is listed under
    <a href="/ecosystem/">Ecosystem</a> when it carries the <code>standardagents</code> keyword.
    Adding <code>provider</code> to the keywords places it with the model providers.
  </p>

  <p class="note">
    To remove a listing, remove the keyword and publish a new version, or unpublish the package
    from npm. The catalogue only mirrors what npm reports.
  </p>
</Base>
